# circleci_insights_flaky_tests (Data Source)

Fetches the flaky tests CircleCI has recorded for a project.

A flake is a test that both passed and failed at the same commit. This is the most directly actionable thing Insights exposes: a `check` block can fail, or an output can be raised, when a project's flake count crosses a budget.

## Availability

| | |
| --- | --- |
| **CircleCI Cloud** | Yes |
| **CircleCI Server** | Depends on the installation. The route is v2, but Insights is a separate service that a given CircleCI Server installation may not run. The provider does not block `deployment = "server"`; if the installation has no Insights, the request fails with a not-found error. |
| **API** | `GET /api/v2/insights/{project-slug}/flaky-tests` |
| **Organization type** | Any. |
| **Token** | An API token with permission to view the project's builds. |

## `total_flaky_tests` is not `length(flaky_tests)`

~> **The two figures count different things, and confusing them will produce a check that never fires or always fires.** `flaky_tests` holds **one entry per flake instance**; `total_flaky_tests` counts **unique tests**. A single test that flaked five times contributes five list entries but one to the total.

Gate on `total_flaky_tests`. Use the list to identify *which* tests and jobs are responsible.

## Nothing to narrow this by

The route takes no parameters beyond the project. Flakes are branch agnostic — there is no branch to scope to — and the retention window is fixed rather than selectable, so this data source has no `branch`, `all_branches` or `reporting_window` argument. It is not paginated either.

A test stops being reported once **two weeks** pass without another flake, and each new flake resets that timer. A project with no entries is either healthy or has not run tests recently; the data source cannot distinguish the two.

## Project slugs are not always `vcs/org/repo`

The `project_slug` argument takes `vcs-slug/org-name/repo-name` — `gh/acme/api` — for GitHub OAuth and Bitbucket projects. **GitLab, GitHub App and GitHub Server projects** have no VCS-side organization and repository name to build a slug from, so their slug is `circleci/<org-uuid>/<project-uuid>`. Both forms are accepted; the `slug` attribute of the `circleci_project` data source reports whichever one applies.

## Accuracy

~> **Insights metrics are recomputed daily**, so a flake from the last 24 hours may not appear yet. See `circleci_insights_workflows` for the full accuracy caveat.

